-- title:
--   Norm string of a diagonal datum over cyclic L/K
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ that is finite and Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by the integer powers of $\sigma$, so that the Galois group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$. Let $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ have vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries, i.e. $t$ is diagonal. Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, where $\mathbb{A}_K$ is the adele ring of $K$, and assume that the image of $\delta$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ induced by the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ coincides with the image of $t$ under the map $\mathrm{GL}_2(L) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ induced by $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ whose $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish, whose $(0,0)$ entry is $\mathrm{N}_{L/K}(t_{00})$ and whose $(1,1)$ entry is $\mathrm{N}_{L/K}(t_{11})$, and such that the norm string of $\delta$, namely the ordered product $\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} \sigma^{(i)}(\delta)$ over $i$ in $\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ with $n = [L:K]$, where $\sigma^{(i)}$ denotes the $i$-fold iterate of the automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ induced by $\sigma$ on the left tensor factor, equals the image of $\gamma$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, the second map being induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$.
--
--   This is the computation, for cyclic $L/K$, that the twisted norm map sends the adelic lift of a diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(t_{00},t_{11}) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ to the diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(\mathrm{N}_{L/K}t_{00}, \mathrm{N}_{L/K}t_{11}) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, so that the $K$-class matching a given split $L$-class is determined by the field norms of its eigenvalues. It is used in the comparison of hyperbolic terms for base change, where the re-indexing of diagonal classes by the norm map is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_diagonal_normString_eq_toTensorGL_globalPoints_of_baseChangeGL_eq_globalPoints.lean

